{"name":"Blue Team Spirit","hex":"#5885a2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"team","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A set of draught animals, such as two horses in front of a carriage.","Any group of people involved in the same activity, especially sports or work."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form a group, as for sports or work.","To go together well; to harmonize."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/team"},{"term":"spirit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The soul of a person or other creature.","A supernatural being, often but not exclusively without physical form; ghost, fairy, angel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To carry off, especially in haste, secrecy, or mystery.","Sometimes followed by up: to animate with vigour; to excite; to encourage; to inspirit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spirit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Team Spirit","blocks":[{"text":"Team Spirit was a joint military training exercise of United States Forces Korea and the Military of South Korea held between 1974 and 1993. The exercise was also scheduled from 1994 to 1996 but cancelled during this time period as part of diplomatic efforts to encourage the Government of North Korea to disable the North Korean nuclear weapons program. The North Korea regime abandoned talks following the January 1986 Team Spirit exercises, and in late 1992, North Korea unilaterally withdrew from the South-North High-Level Talks due to the 1993 Team Spirit exercise."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/ROKAF_and_USAF_fighters_during_Team_Spirit_84.JPEG/330px-ROKAF_and_USAF_fighters_during_Team_Spirit_84.JPEG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Team_Spirit"},{"title":"Team building","blocks":[{"text":"Team building is a collective term for various interventions that improve team effectiveness and define roles within teams, often involving collaborative tasks. It is distinct from team training, which is designed by a combination of business managers, learning and development/OD and an HR Business Partner to improve the efficiency, rather than interpersonal relations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/US_Navy_040518-N-9693M-015_A_squad_of_Midshipmen_work_with_a_log_as_part_of_teamwork_training_during_Sea_Trials.jpg/330px-US_Navy_040518-N-9693M-015_A_squad_of_Midshipmen_work_with_a_log_as_part_of_teamwork_training_during_Sea_Trials.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Team_building"},{"title":"Team","blocks":[{"text":"A team is a group of individuals working together to achieve their goal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Team_work.jpg/330px-Team_work.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Team"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Monts-merveilles.fr_teambuilding.jpg/500px-Monts-merveilles.fr_teambuilding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Monts-merveilles.fr_teambuilding.jpg/1280px-Monts-merveilles.fr_teambuilding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Monts-merveilles.fr_teambuilding.jpg/500px-Monts-merveilles.fr_teambuilding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"These teams have built small ocean-going rafts as part of a team-building exercise.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonts-merveilles.fr_teambuilding.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Team_building_strategies_as_described_by_Klein.png/500px-Team_building_strategies_as_described_by_Klein.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Team_building_strategies_as_described_by_Klein.png/500px-Team_building_strategies_as_described_by_Klein.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Effects of team building strategies on all four outcomes, with 10% and 90% credibility intervals[12]\n","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATeam_building_strategies_as_described_by_Klein.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Type_91_SAM_fire.JPG/500px-Type_91_SAM_fire